+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Token and stored-token files use mode 0600. The port secures an existing
file through its descriptor before truncation or writing; a permission
failure now aborts the write instead of updating an exposed token file.
Keep the configured token directory private and owned by the invoking user.

CLI extensions and subprocess-backed helpers run with the invoking user's
authority. The remote Jobs sandbox is not a local OpenBSD process sandbox.
